{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517906-conspiracy-theory-compacts","id":1517906,"title":"Conspiracy Theory: Compacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-13T17:40:06-07:00","id":1517906,"title":"Conspiracy Theory: Compacts","content":"So I didn't plan on starting this thread so early, and I am not sure I am going to actually go deep into it immediately after this post, but it is a scratch that I have to itch and so this is what we are doing- the &quot;Step 0&quot; of this part of the project. The Culling.<br /> <br /> I mean, there are two main reasons why it is simply unrealistic to go through all compacts for this project- first, the sheer number of them. Compacts serve as the majority of Hunter orgs, and so while covering all conspiracies is realistic, covering all compacts to the same level would be a hell of a headache to me. However, I would probably have done so- if I were to think it is appropriate. Thankfully, it is not the case- most compacts are really not &quot;conspiracy material&quot;. They don't cover the same reach and require the same lore as conspiracies. Sure, each could benefit from a C&amp;C like treatment, and each also has its own secrets, yet having a weird masterplan to take over the world and/or the potential to use supernatural abilities? Yeah, that's a bit much, especially for fella such as the Union. Compacts are generally compacts for a reason, and most of the time, it should stay that way.<br /> <br /> But sometimes, there is a diamond in the rough- one which could be polished into something much more... interesting.<br /> <br /> So in here, we are going to go through all canon compacts and decide which one should be treated gain the &quot;conspiracy treatment&quot; and who shouldn't. Obviously, I am open for your feedback on the subject, but I am currently going to judge using the following criteria, ranked by the order of significance:<br /> <br /> <b>A) Text-</b> in a few rare instances, the text itself suggests &quot;this org could be a conspiracy&quot;. In such instances, I obviously will include the compact in the project regardless of other factors.<br /> <br /> <b>B) Endowment Material-</b> generally, that refers to some supernatural ability a compact holds, which might be developed to a full blown Endowments, even though that scientific/mundane tools could also qualify if they are viewed as worthy enough. This includes, potentially, a &quot;supernatural origin&quot; of the hunters, even though it is not a common thing for compacts (those are already conspiracies, generally). It should be noted that even if that in those instances, even if the compact itself can't be developed into a conspiracy, there is the potential for its potential Endowments to serve as a base for another which may achieve it, and as such are worthy to be examined.<br /> <br /> <b>C) Structure-</b> not all conspiracies have a structure, but those with it are definitely in a better position to serve as such. 2e, for some reason, have focused a lot around fractured and small scale conspiracies, which, heh, I have some opinions on it, but regardless structure on its own may serve as a good base for a conspiracy, especially if it allows the compact to extract its power and grow beyond its limits.<br /> <br /> <b>D) Patron-</b> when a conspiracy is fractured, it generally means that something holds it together- and generally the conspiracy itself doesn't fully understand who controls it from the shadow. Compacts who are sponsored by some entity, be it supernatural or otherwise, could potentially develop to a global scale depending on the interests of the patron, which means it is something we should consider.<br /> <br /> <b>E) Age-</b> compacts are found in a metastable state. Most don't survive more than a few decades. A compact which, according to its canon, have survived for quite some time, is probably on the edge of becoming something greater than itself- and as such could potentially start working in their own secret plan for the future.<br /> <br /> <b>F) Vibes-</b> the most fluffy test which is why it is in the bottom of the list, yet also important on its own, &quot;vibes&quot; basically refer the to the feeling of the compact- does it resonate with some real life conspiracy theory bs? Does it feel like it is occult and significant? Does it have a weight in the setting which should be considered? Because it is so fluffy, it is subject to personal interpretation, so I am going to avoid judging according to vibes alone, and which is why the fact that the compact is being loved by someone is not enough for it to be a conspiracy.<br /> <br /> <b>S) Uniqueness-</b> this &quot;special&quot; test is here to make things more complicated and annoying for everyone. Before 2e, I would not have considered this test, yet 2e have added the very cool concept of chapters- basically, &quot;regional variants&quot; of conspiracies. Conspiracies, after all, are global entities, which means that localization is an essential part of it. <i>Unfortunately</i>, this concept remains as just that- a concept. We only have 2 actual examples of chapters, none of which is actually called as such- the Otodo and the Order of the Black Knight. Potentially, we could also include things like the Society of the 12 Keys or the Swords of Jibril to the mix, but that's more &quot;iffy&quot;. Regardless, this means that if a certain compacts works well on all categories, yet lacks enough narrative weight to be distinguished as a conspiracy from another one, I would consider it to be a chapter instead its own conspiracy. I do plan to examining chapters as well, but that is a subject for a future thread. Obviously, this test is also somewhat subjective, so opinions may vary on this one.<br /> <br /> So with that in mind, let's see what the 2nd Tier has to offer, shall we?<br /> <br /> <b><u>1e Core</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey:</b> a easy yes. They answer criteria A (C&amp;C suggests that they technically have the resources and means to be a conspiracy if they'll just stop just being a pyramid scheme), C (the whole license system), D (someone is standing at the head of the pyramid), E (dating all the way from 1855, so they are more than a 100 years old) and F (&quot;rich people having a secret murderous society&quot; falls within the tropes of conspiracy theories, and in 2e they are stated to have absorbed other compacts, so if a compact has chapters, isn't it basically a conspiracy?). One could even argue that the Bacchanal could serve as answering B, and they are definitely unique enough to answer S.<br /> <br /> <b>Long Night:</b> a bit more complicate case. The Prayer Endowment that they have in C&amp;C feels proper enough to answer B, but the rest is a bit of problematic. Protestantism is a very varied branch in Christianity, and the Long Night basically rides this part all way home in C&amp;C, which make C into an issue and the rest on extension.. but things are a bit different when Dark Eras is taken into account. While the Long Night as we know it trace its origin to around 1970, Dark Eras 2 actually extends it much further, to the time of the Scandinavian Witch Trails if not beforehand. Now, it is very likely that the Long Night of that period was very different from the modern version- especially as, considering the region and time period, we are talking about Lutheran version of the org, which is likely to still exist in Europe in modern times, and Lutheranism is much more structured compared to other Protestant Churches (even if not to the degree Catholicism is). As such, it is possible that the Long Night is either a local chapter of a wider conspiracy, or an incarnation of a fallen conspiracy, which would answer C and E criteria, while still maintaining enough degree of uniqueness- so it answers a majority of the criteria and as such gets a place on the list.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule:</b> another very easy yes. They have structure and hierarchy under the Three Old Men so they answer C, date to the Thule Society so they have passed the 100 years (which answers E), deal constantly with the occult and include material on ghost-bound pistoles and summoning rites of root-race ghosts (B), have a lot of conspiracy vibes (I mean, occult Nazis? Do you need more?), and potentially even have some God Machine influence (D) as per the Cold War Dark Era, not to mention that they definitely answer the S test of uniqueness. So yeah, they easily get a spot on this list.<br /> \u200b<br /> <b>Network 0:</b> so they get an immediate &quot;yes&quot; as they answer the A test- C&amp;C outright present the possibility of them becoming a conspiracy, which also answers B by extension. As such, other tests are really just overkill and aren't really needed in that case.<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis: </b>a more complicated case, the Null Mysteriis seem to answer the B test as their C&amp;C Endowment does feel more like a &quot;true Endowment&quot;, or at least, the base for one. Additionally, they answer the Age test, being around 130 years old. They also seem to have enough organization to have competing factions within them, and the academy does lend itself into structured hierarchies, so C is also being answered to a sufficient degree. They are also definitely unique, so S is maintained. The main problem with them, however, is F- they just don't really have the vibes for a conspiracy. On the other hand, Campion are a conspiracy, so.. I don't know, I need to think about it more.<br /> <br /> <b>Union:</b> and easy no. The fact that they are 2nd Tier is an achievement on its own, and they basically fail every test- which is a good thing. They don't want to be a conspiracy, after all.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Witch Finders</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Division Six:</b> a bit of a oddball. While they have some structure, they are still a bunch of conspiracy theorists being manipulated by a Seer, so I assume that they are getting C (like, barely) and definitely get D. Their &quot;extreme conditioning&quot; could qualify as B, and they have around 47 years- which is a bit short for me to let them take E, but some may argue otherwise. The God Machine knows that TtF gave us younger conspiracies- but you probably know what I think of that. The main problem is whether they have the vibes, and more importantly, that A actively goes against it, with describing them as being absorbed by TFV. So.. yeah, really on the fence, and if B and D weren't on the table I would have just dropped them from the list on A alone.<br /> <br /> <b>Keepers of the Source:</b> those guys have a really strong B, I must say- the Dowsing Sense really fits the criteria, especially is they are indeed Lucid. They also have some support from F in terms of their description in BotD and the fact they got republished in 2e. They are definitely unique, and barely pass the Age criteria (53 years). Sure, they also have a lot against them, but I would argue that B alone would make it worthwhile to put them on the list.<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean Brotherhood:</b> easy yes, text already gives us everything we need, not to mention B from the Rite of Hecate, already described C, being apparently a incarnation of an older organization (E) and so forth. <br /> <br /> <b><u>Spirit Slayers</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Bear Lodge:</b> found in the same problem as Division Six- A is outright against them, mentioning that they have been absorbed to the Ashwood Abbey. If we are to ignore it, they do seem to have some material for Endowment from their Unseen Senses and reduced Lunacy (B) and some structure (C) and are over 100 years old (E). Honestly, I think that they are unique enough from the Abbey to stand on their own, so if A wasn't an issue I would have given them easy S, but A puts some very heavy burden here so... yeah, need to think about it.<br /> <br /> <b>Illuminated Brotherhood:</b> definitely have B, between the special connection they develop to the spirit world through drug use and the strange drugs they synthesis. Not sure about C, and are a bit short from getting the E criteria. I also think that their main problem is S- the use of drugs to see the truth has some strong overlap with alchemy (see M:tAs Solifacti), which puts them as having much more sense as a spirit-focused chapter of the AO than its own conspiracy.<br /> <br /> <b>Talbot Group:</b> not really have a lot going for them, actually. Serving as a support group for monsters is a interesting niche, sure, but I'm not sure they have much in the other criteria. The main thing they have standing for them is B, yet their supernatural benefits are almost identical to the Bear Lodge- so if they get the conspiracy treatment instead of the chapter treatment, this compact has nothing in their favor. Not sure if they should be a chapter of the Survivors Club- they have some overlap, but maybe they'll work better with some other group...<br /> <br /> <b><u>Night Stalkers</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Barrett Commission:</b>a wasted potential in terms of A- like, seriously, outside of that they really have a lot going for them. Excellent C, E, F and S. I would have given them easy spot on the list, but the text claiming that they have been absorbed by TFV is annoying. Also, makes even less sense compared to Division Six, where the logic was already shaky. Really consider to give them a spot regardless of A. <br /> <br /> <b>Maiden's Blood Sisterhood:</b> their connection to witches and the occult gives them a decent score for B, which also answers D by extension. They also seem to have enough structure to answer C, and are around 66 years old so I am willing to give them E. They do have overlap with the Survivors Club, however, so I need to give it thought (even though they are a good excuse for adapting a Cruac version for Hunter).<br /> <br /> <b>Night Watch:</b> yeah, no. Community guards and all of that, really don't feel like they have something beyond of that.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Slasher</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Hunt Club:</b> yeah, no. Basically fail on S on being similar to the Abbey, as they only answer the rest of the criteria as good as the Abbey does and on the same metric- only being less player friendly. So yeah, no.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Mortal Remains</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Habibti Maa:</b> have some interesting things going on for them. There seems to be some supernatural benefit for their deprogramming techniques, which answers B, and they have Maat as their patron (which could indicate some involvement by the Judges), so we have D. I also think that C is also on the table for them. They are young, however, and not sure about vibes- but hey, we could also make the Talbot Group into a chapter of those if we want to. So I tend towards a positive answer.<br /> <br /> <b>Reckoning:</b> easy no, basically fail uniqueness for the Long Night and have little to no support for any other criteria. <br /> <br /> <b>Yuri's Group:</b> again, fail on S towards the Survivors Club, and all else falls apart accordingly.<br /> <br /> <b>Utopia Now:</b> succeed on A- 2e mentions them as a conspiracy, and while it might have been a errata issue, I have intentionally not submitted it as an issue just so that we will have a canon support for this claim, and it seems that everyone else have done the same. Yes, they also answer other criteria, but A is enough.<br /> <br /> <b><u>2e Core</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Nine Stars:</b> basically a re-iteration of VASCU with less resources, so even if they were to have any argument in their favor, they would still fall, at best case scenario, as VASCU's chapter.<br /> <br /> <b>SWORN:</b> interesting case. They seem to be on the edge of the E test, but they also seem to connect to the Keepers of the Weave, which shows a longer tradition. They do have global presence, so they have C to a sufficient degree, and they are unique enough, but not sure about vibes. Considering that the KotW also weren't a conspiracy, there isn't much support for B (even though I headcanon otherwise), so I need to think about it.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Tending the Fire</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Crimson Halo:</b> on one hand, they are community guardians. On the other, they answer the criteria much better than any other similar group. They have some answer for C, and answer E as good as any compact could, having more than 100 years on their side. They are also unique, but lack in the other fields. I would have to think about it, yet it might just be because I really love them.<br /> <br /> <b>Crossroads Convoy:</b> the main point we have for them is C- they definitely have some level of organization. About everything else... we have no date so we know nothing about E, and the only way to justify B for them is by stealing the original covenant benefit for the Gallows Post. Unfortunately, I don't think they make the cut.<br /> <br /> <b>Eden Covenant:</b> yeah, no. Best case scenario they are a Long Night chapter.<br /> <br /> <b>Las Guadanas:</b> a big fat yes. Medium merit at 3 dots gives them B, have structure through the cartels and such so C, Santa Muerta gives D, going all the way back to Aztec Death Cults gives E, they have some great vibes for F and their attitude towards death is very different from the CoB so they also get S. In fact, they remind me a lot of my own homebrew Ebony Fangs, so it would give me an opportunity to discuss them through this compact so.. yeah, definitely on the list.<br /> <br /> <b>Recalibrators:</b> feel like a bit of small scale. They have some organization for C, but not sure about the rest. Anyway, even as a conspiracy they'll move between TFV territory and the Sanitation Collective from, Light &amp; Dark, so I tend to exclude them from the list.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Dark Eras</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Ama San:</b> their whole Whale Whistle thing gives some excellent B to work with, so even though they fail on most other criteria (I think that C and E may be argued for), I would tend to give them a spot here.<br /> <br /> <b>Azusa Miko:</b> while they definitely answer all criteria to a very satisfying degree, their attitude makes them feel very close to the CoB, which would likely make them more of a chapter of the conspiracy in this regard, and as such they unfortunately do not get to the list.<br /> <br /> <b>Bijin:</b> if they still exist, it is likely they do as a AA chapter, failing on uniqueness here.<br /> <br /> <b>Followers of Mansa:</b> while cool in principle, and while they have been presented with enough structure to answer C and likely have enough Age for E in their Era, I am not sure they have enough on the other criteria to stand, unfortunately. <br /> <br /> <b>Gumi:</b> while they have structure and some age, I am not sure they have enough on the other parameters. So yeah, did I just included cut material just to ignore it again? Yeah, but we should remember that those guys almost were in the book.<br /> <br /> <b>Keepers of the Weave:</b> same state as SWORN, being entangled with them.<br /> <br /> <b>Les Voyageurs:</b> fail on S towards the Bear Lodge and potentially S^2 if the Lodge is part of the Abbey.<br /> <br /> <b>Protectors of the Light:</b> community guardians who fail like most of those groups, unless they have some legacy in SWORN.<br /> <br /> <b>Scarlet Watch:</b> a almost definite yes. Their writeup heavily suggest that they are a fallen conspiracy, and all of the dream-fate-blood-bond thing they have going on is a strong base for B. E and F also work within their Era, and it seems that at least in the past they had C, even if they are more fractured within their Era. Also, very unique IMO, getting easy pass on S.<br /> <br /> <b>Soldiers of the Forbidden Sun:</b> having more than 1400 years on their side during their own Era, it is a wordcount-caused warcrime that they are not being presented as a conspiracy in the first place. Like, by E alone they should be a conspiracy, not to mention the vibes from F, structure from C, and some base with Taoism for B. It is possible to make them a eastern AO chapter, but they feel distinct enough to stand on their own.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Other</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Ahl al Jabal:</b> they have a lot going for them to be considered, including B (occult interests), C, E and F- yet they have issues with S. The fact that they are being based on the Hashashins, and the AO being based around the same concept, puts them in a awkward state when considered as a conspiracy. They may work better as a AO chapter in this regard, but subject for change.<br /> <br /> <b>Heritage House:</b> honestly, their writeup is so similar to the Scarlet Watch that they sound like their modern incarnation- so yes by extension.<br /> <br /> *********************************<br /> <br /> And that's for stage 0. I'll return later to this thread after giving some though about who actually makes it through the list, but feel free to give feedback about those estimations- note that I want to trim the list as much as possible, so a lot of edge cases may fall eventually if I won't see good enough reason to keep them (hence why I will be listening to suggestions, to a degree).<br /> <br /> Anyway, see you next time!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T18:43:37-07:00","id":1517907,"title":"","content":"All compacts and conspiracies deserve a C&amp;C treatment lol (I may try and write one for 9 stars and Bear Lodge)<br /> <br /> Anyway, i disagree with your stance on the talbot Group. They have structure, and have a clear goal, which is to cure monsters, NOT support them. All there work is spent on this, and is noted as being downright disturbing to see (which is why such facilities are in a remote location). I don't see them being absorbed by the Survivors Club, whos Endowment represents a deep empathy with the monster inside, rather than need to cure it.<br /> <br /> I think they fulfill A and C. B is possible, and their faction the Councilliators could find something. I also believe their actions could gain a patron in the Shadow, pun intended. My head canon on the redactors looking into the spirit world also opens up a possible reconciliation between the two factions to gain from each other, but that's headcanon so sorry for rambling. I do think S and F are up to the indiviual, but of Yuri's group and habibti ma, I do see the Talbot group as above them in S (about even with habiti ma though)<br /> <br /> Otherwise love what you have. Oh, and yeah, ignore A on Barret Commission. They deserve it. I'm biased and I love those cold hearted assholes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T20:34:11-07:00","id":1517909,"title":"","content":"Re: A: As previously, I have to point out that the text on the Barrett Commission is that they were split up and that there are <i>theories</i> that they were merged into TFV (the text simply stating that TFV is the only official government-sanctioned hunter conspiracy in an edition where being separated from the FBI didn't stop VASCU from continuing to exist), this being part of a discussion of how speculation in general is more widespread than fact among hunters and specifically that some hunters think governments and other ruling bodies lending their support to compacts and conspiracies in an uneven fashion is responsible for those groups' changing fates.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I can literally find nothing in the text saying that the Bear Lodge was absorbed into the Abbey \u2014 Hunter 2e has two books out, the Bear Lodge is mentioned in one paragraph of the corebook (right before the bit you're looking at about Div 6 and the Commission), and that paragraph is there talking about how the group might have an older pedigree than surmised and evidence suggests its hunters are still around <i>despite</i> rumors of its collapse.<br /> <br /> This is all from a section of the corebook talking about how hunters don't have the complete picture of their supernatural-adjacent culture's past and present, and while I have some issues with bits of 2e treating conspiracies like open secrets, &quot;a shadow organization with notable resources and an agenda may have recruited or formed out of this regional association of hunters that we haven't heard from in a while&quot; is a good continuation of all the stuff 1e established about hunters being rightly paranoid, hunter groups being susceptible to compromise by the supernatural, and higher tiers of organization tending to quietly watch and/or manipulate the lower ones to save their own resources and/or further their agendas.<br /> <br /> That this continued harping on about stuff that didn't happen to the stated degree (or didn't happen at all) is giving me powerful recollections of people thinking the Beast Kickstarter draft was comparing the Begotten to minorities because it mentioned the phenomenon of othering in an explanation of how the Temenos relates to factuality does not make me inclined to stop pointing out that the complaints are based in unfounded or exaggerated views of the material.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd contend that Division 6, the Bear Lodge, and Habibti Ma don't have solid grounds for Endowments, seeing as Unseen Sense is a core Merit and both editions of the game have a core Tactic for helping deprogram supernatural mental influence out of people \u2014 an Endowment is generally more than 1e Werewolf's Wolf-Blooded package.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T20:51:37-07:00","id":1517910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517906-conspiracy-theory-compacts?p=1517909#post1517909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: A: As previously, I have to point out that the text on the Barrett Commission is that they were split up and that there are <i>theories</i> that they were merged into TFV (the text simply stating that TFV is the only official government-sanctioned hunter conspiracy in an edition where being separated from the FBI didn't stop VASCU from continuing to exist), this being part of a discussion of how speculation in general is more widespread than fact among hunters and specifically that some hunters think governments and other ruling bodies lending their support to compacts and conspiracies in an uneven fashion is responsible for those groups' changing fates.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I can literally find nothing in the text saying that the Bear Lodge was absorbed into the Abbey \u2014 Hunter 2e has two books out, the Bear Lodge is mentioned in one paragraph of the corebook (right before the bit you're looking at about Div 6 and the Commission), and that paragraph is there talking about how the group might have an older pedigree than surmised and evidence suggests its hunters are still around <i>despite</i> rumors of its collapse.<br /> <br /> This is all from a section of the corebook talking about how hunters don't have the complete picture of their supernatural-adjacent culture's past and present, and while I have some issues with bits of 2e treating conspiracies like open secrets, &quot;a shadow organization with notable resources and an agenda may have recruited or formed out of this regional association of hunters that we haven't heard from in a while&quot; is a good continuation of all the stuff 1e established about hunters being rightly paranoid, hunter groups being susceptible to compromise by the supernatural, and higher tiers of organization tending to quietly watch and/or manipulate the lower ones to save their own resources and/or further their agendas.<br /> <br /> That this continued harping on about stuff that didn't happen to the stated degree (or didn't happen at all) is giving me powerful recollections of people thinking the Beast Kickstarter draft was comparing the Begotten to minorities because it mentioned the phenomenon of othering in an explanation of how the Temenos relates to factuality does not make me inclined to stop pointing out that the complaints are based in unfounded or exaggerated views of the material.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd contend that Division 6, the Bear Lodge, and Habibti Ma don't have solid grounds for Endowments, seeing as Unseen Sense is a core Merit and both editions of the game have a core Tactic for helping deprogram supernatural mental influence out of people \u2014 an Endowment is generally more than 1e Werewolf's Wolf-Blooded package.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points. However may I ask your contention with division 6? The ability to intentionally utilize Paradox to force Fallen laws to suppress magic is unique to them, plus they have the patron for possible conspiracy status (plus I'm biased toward a possible scenario where Mr Jones Ascends and rewards division 6 by making their fake history become real).<br /> <br /> Also, I think (sorry if I'm misrepresenting you LostLight) Light arguing those compacts because while Unseen sense is a common merit, their existence as a status effect implies a compact is tapping into something supernatural, which is pre-requisite toward Endowments if I'm correct","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T21:34:47-07:00","id":1517913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517906-conspiracy-theory-compacts?p=1517910#post1517910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good points. However may I ask your contention with division 6? The ability to intentionally utilize Paradox to force Fallen laws to suppress magic is unique to them,</div> </div> </div> </div>They make the Paradox penalty imposed by their observation of magic one die worse in Witch Finders' Gutter Magic systems. Liar is a one-dot Merit in Mage 2e that makes a Sleeper who has it add two dice to Paradox risk instead of one and add two dice to the Integrity roll for Dissonance against spells whose effects they witness.<br /> <br /> Liar is from the same section of the Mage 2e corebook where other Merits suggested as workarounds for a Hunter game dealing with the Awakened, like Strained or Fitful Slumber, are printed, and they are assumedly common enough to be printed in the corebook's section on Sleepers and Sleepwalkers instead of in a Night Horrors writeup or other unique circumstance \u2014 a character who makes Paradox worse around them due to their indoctrination as a mid-level dupe of the Exarchs is not what I would describe as uniquely empowered to the level of having a category of monster-hunting aid that can benefit from R&amp;D by itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I think (sorry if I'm misrepresenting you LostLight) Light arguing those compacts because while Unseen sense is a common merit, their existence as a status effect implies a compact is tapping into something supernatural, which is pre-requisite toward Endowments if I'm correct </div> </div> </div>If there is something consistent that Advanced Armory is tapping into beyond &quot;application of advanced science in a setting where spiritual possession can alter your biology and ritual magic can take many forms&quot; I am eager to hear it, but broadly speaking Endowments run the gamut from using supernatural effects to including things that can even the playing field with regards to certain types of supernatural obstacle rather than necessarily and specifically tapping into supernatural patronage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T21:43:47-07:00","id":1517914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517906-conspiracy-theory-compacts?p=1517913#post1517913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They make the Paradox penalty imposed by their observation of magic one die worse in Witch Finders' Gutter Magic systems. Liar is a one-dot Merit in Mage 2e that makes a Sleeper who has it add two dice to Paradox risk instead of one and add two dice to the Integrity roll for Dissonance against spells whose effects they witness.<br /> <br /> Liar is from the same section of the Mage 2e corebook where other Merits suggested as workarounds for a Hunter game dealing with the Awakened, like Strained or Fitful Slumber, are printed, and they are assumedly common enough to be printed in the corebook's section on Sleepers and Sleepwalkers instead of in a Night Horrors writeup or other unique circumstance \u2014 a character who makes Paradox worse around them due to their indoctrination as a mid-level dupe of the Exarchs is not what I would describe as uniquely empowered to the level of having a category of monster-hunting aid that can benefit from R&amp;D by itself.<br /> <br /> If there is something consistent that Advanced Armory is tapping into beyond &quot;application of advanced science in a setting where spiritual possession can alter your biology and ritual magic can take many forms&quot; I am eager to hear it, but broadly speaking Endowments run the gamut from using supernatural effects to including things that can even the playing field with regards to certain types of supernatural obstacle rather than necessarily and specifically tapping into supernatural patronage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha on division 6, though I'd argue it sets them on the PATH toward an Endowment. Obviously by itself it's nothing. But Ascending ones used to just poison themselves and get powered up, and it was later developed into an Endowment.<br /> <br /> hmm, interesting argument with Advanced armory, but I thought all the Endowments were heavily implied to be supernatural? Unless you are specifically speaking bout the patronage part? I'm not saying an Endowment needs patronage, but that in of itself need be supernatural or at least directly manipulating it. Though Campion Endowment exists","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T22:07:37-07:00","id":1517915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517906-conspiracy-theory-compacts?p=1517914#post1517914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotcha on division 6, though I'd argue it sets them on the PATH toward an Endowment. Obviously by itself it's nothing. But Ascending ones used to just poison themselves and get powered up, and it was later developed into an Endowment.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lore about Elixirs is that they were alchemical concoctions mixed with poison and tempered/purified with the appropriate internal processes. It's a form of magic codified enough to warrant treating an Endowment, because Elixirs is as much about <i>not getting poisoned</i> as it is deriving supernatural effects from a volatile collection of substances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> hmm, interesting argument with Advanced armory, but I thought all the Endowments were heavily implied to be supernatural? </div> </div> </div>The second sentence of 2e's section on Endowments begins &quot;While not always inherently supernatural,&quot; and then describes them as allowing hunters to deal with the supernatural on their level. The 1e lexicon described them as &quot;supernatural or high-tech.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless you are specifically speaking bout the patronage part? I'm not saying an Endowment needs patronage, but that in of itself need be supernatural or at least directly manipulating it. Though Campion Endowment exists </div> </div> </div>While you might be able to make some intimations based on the presence of the adjective &quot;etheric&quot; in one description of its power source, the Mjolnir Cannon is functionally a battery-powered super-taser. While the detailed description wasn't carried over to the 2e writeup, a VDSB works on phosphorescent lights and focusing mirrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T22:18:32-07:00","id":1517917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517906-conspiracy-theory-compacts?p=1517915#post1517915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lore about Elixirs is that they were alchemical concoctions mixed with poison and tempered/purified with the appropriate internal processes. It's a form of magic codified enough to warrant treating an Endowment, because Elixirs is as much about <i>not getting poisoned</i> as it is deriving supernatural effects from a volatile collection of substances.<br /> <br /> The second sentence of 2e's section on Endowments begins &quot;While not always inherently supernatural,&quot; and then describes them as allowing hunters to deal with the supernatural on their level. The 1e lexicon described them as &quot;supernatural or high-tech.&quot;<br /> <br /> While you might be able to make some intimations based on the presence of the adjective &quot;etheric&quot; in one description of its power source, the Mjolnir Cannon is functionally a battery-powered super-taser. While the detailed description wasn't carried over to the 2e writeup, a VDSB works on phosphorescent lights and focusing mirrors.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point with elixirs was at one point in the Ascending ones infancy, the internal alchemy part of it didn't exist. 2nd edition is explicit they were just poisoning themselves before (and almost died off because of it)<br /> <br /> Ehh, while not inherently supernatural, thats like saying advanced armory isnt supernatural because because compound rounds are shot out of a regular gun. There's a reason their Endowment is very fishy in their descriptions. Despite the definition, every Endowment has been shown to be supernatural in some way until Campion. But alas, that is the word of the corebook, so I'm inclined to say you're right.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T23:00:26-07:00","id":1517920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517906-conspiracy-theory-compacts?p=1517917#post1517917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point with elixirs was at one point in the Ascending ones infancy, the internal alchemy part of it didn't exist. 2nd edition is explicit they were just poisoning themselves before (and almost died off because of it)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because I have a lot of my headspace currently occupied by the Followers/Cult of Typhon-/Set, and correspondingly the Cult of the Phoenix and the Ascending Ones, I need to comment that Elixirs existed in the early Cult of the Phoenix most likely as an emergency basis rather a regular practice. The original mention of their implementation of proto-Elixirs, while arguably a case of deliberate mythologizing a particular moment in time in the middle of a historical confession to hide further truths, assumes they just had an elixir to deny them sleep (which I will not be glib and just call coffee) as a readily understood practice, but was a response to the Cult of the Phoenix stepping into the night. If either of the two cults was regularly poisoning itself, it was the Cult of Set, while the Cult of the Phoenix maybe had Elixirs as an emergency, but if they practiced like a Conspiracy likely had a different, if connected, Endowment. A particular point of note is that, in that the Ascending Ones explores there own idea of duality, the notion of poison extends beyond the tempering of Elixirs and seems to have entered the Ascending Ones as a hold over from the Cult of Set as the conspiracy went from the two times of day being assigned a cult of monster hunters to a hunter organization representing the entire 24-hour cycle.<br /> <br /> As it relates to the larger argument, I have nothing to add but &quot;They're one of the few on my 'actually fuzzy' list of Kin for Beast, but the longer I go on, the more certain I am that the Ascending Ones, at least, are on the Kin side of that knife.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T04:52:05-07:00","id":1517935,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24173\" data-vbnamecard=\"24173\">Primordial newcomer</a> yes, I agree that every compact could benefit from C&amp;C treatment (I have said much in the post), the question here is obviously different, as those threads explore the idea of &quot;world wide manipulation plan&quot;, which is a harsher criteria overall. About Talbot Group- I have actually referred to the Habibti Maa, not the Survivors Club. The whole process of conditioning and reprogramming have narrative overlap to the same degree the Otodo and the Lucifuge have, or the Order of the Black Knight and the AKD have. It should be noted that with the chapter system (as far as I can understand it), becoming a chapter does not make a compact to lose its identity or cease to exist- from what we have, chapters seem to have a lot of independence, so suggesting that a compact would become a chapter does not mean &quot;they are destroyed&quot;. Again, I would have loved to actually get this concept more developed in 2e, but this seems to be the direction the text suggests.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> I have worked from memory during a very late hour, so the Kickstarter draft was bleeding into my mind during the process. It should be noted that while the final version does not explicitly mentions the fall of those compacts, for the purpose of this project the strong implicit suggestions by the text are enough to at the very least consider it as a factor. Also, I understand you are coming from the point of &quot;fighting misinformation&quot;, but I would appreciate if you would be clearer about it from the get go from the first sentence, as this was a honest mistake from my part and your post felt a bit aggressive which made it difficult to me to actually read it. Not that I am saying you meant to be aggressive, but it just makes me harder to read through your posts, which is unfortunate as you usually have good things to add to the discussion. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T08:10:59-07:00","id":1517940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517906-conspiracy-theory-compacts?p=1517935#post1517935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24173\" data-vbnamecard=\"24173\">Primordial newcomer</a> yes, I agree that every compact could benefit from C&amp;C treatment (I have said much in the post), the question here is obviously different, as those threads explore the idea of &quot;world wide manipulation plan&quot;, which is a harsher criteria overall. About Talbot Group- I have actually referred to the Habibti Maa, not the Survivors Club. The whole process of conditioning and reprogramming have narrative overlap to the same degree the Otodo and the Lucifuge have, or the Order of the Black Knight and the AKD have. It should be noted that with the chapter system (as far as I can understand it), becoming a chapter does not make a compact to lose its identity or cease to exist- from what we have, chapters seem to have a lot of independence, so suggesting that a compact would become a chapter does not mean &quot;they are destroyed&quot;. Again, I would have loved to actually get this concept more developed in 2e, but this seems to be the direction the text suggests.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> I have worked from memory during a very late hour, so the Kickstarter draft was bleeding into my mind during the process. It should be noted that while the final version does not explicitly mentions the fall of those compacts, for the purpose of this project the strong implicit suggestions by the text are enough to at the very least consider it as a factor. Also, I understand you are coming from the point of &quot;fighting misinformation&quot;, but I would appreciate if you would be clearer about it from the get go from the first sentence, as this was a honest mistake from my part and your post felt a bit aggressive which made it difficult to me to actually read it. Not that I am saying you meant to be aggressive, but it just makes me harder to read through your posts, which is unfortunate as you usually have good things to add to the discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I understand your intention with the culling Light. I was just saying I would love C&amp;C for them all. Apart from that, it make sense that not all compacts have the means or motivation to influence the world to such a degree.<br /> <br /> As for Talbot group, hmm. Ill admit they have grown on me a lot over the years. Maybe I'm biased to see them standing on their own. I believe their status as redeemers hits a different note than lucifuge, even if it's a similar sounding one. Also, just want to say habibti ma is a great example of a mundane organization just now becoming a hunter compact. I think this inexperience could lead to talbot group being the one to absorb them, as they have a lot more supernatural knowledge.<br /> <br /> im not against the chapter system, i think its very cool! I just dont like seeing it happen to preexisting compacts since it gets rid of their factions and changes their focus a bit along with independence. That's strictly a me problem though, and honestly your choices for what become chapters does it make sense.<br /> <br /> also, I'm surprised you didn't mention the Pursuit looking into Bacchanalia as an endowment, though I wonder if the Abbey would manage to retain enough members if they decided to give them actual tasks rather than have fun however they see fit<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T03:51:34-07:00","id":1518231,"title":"","content":"So after giving it some thought, the list of examined Compacts will be-<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey<br /> Loyalists of Thule<br /> Network 0<br /> Keepers of the Source<br /> Promethean Brotherhood<br /> Bear Lodge<br /> Barrett Commission<br /> Maiden's Blood Sisterhood<br /> Habibti Maa<br /> Utopia Now<br /> Ama San<br /> Soldiers of the Forbidden Sun<br /> Heritage House<br /> SWORN<br /> Las Guadanas<br /> <br /> I may throw tweak the list during the project, but this is the plan at least. I will take probably a few more days before I'll start dealing with it, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T06:36:49-07:00","id":1518238,"title":"","content":"Nice list. Shocked the Bear Lodge made it. Don't get me wrong I love those guys. I should say pleasantly shocked.<br /> <br /> the truest Hunters. Time to settle the title for Apex Predator.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Was the lack of organization what did the Long Night in? They are the compact, hell one of the hunter orgs period, with the clearest goal in mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 07-18-2023, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T08:19:52-07:00","id":1518242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517906-conspiracy-theory-compacts?p=1518238#post1518238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: Was the lack of organization what did the Long Night in? They are the compact, hell one of the hunter orgs period, with the clearest goal in mind</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly because their main factor for considering them have conspiracy-like traits based around relation to a Lutheran equivalent which exists in DE2, but the focus on the Long Night on the Rapture which, from what I can gather, is not a strong feature of Lutheran Christianity puts them on a shakey ground. I may add them in the future, but I need time to think how to deal with that part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T08:52:22-07:00","id":1518248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517906-conspiracy-theory-compacts?p=1518242#post1518242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mostly because their main factor for considering them have conspiracy-like traits based around relation to a Lutheran equivalent which exists in DE2, but the focus on the Long Night on the Rapture which, from what I can gather, is not a strong feature of Lutheran Christianity puts them on a shakey ground. I may add them in the future, but I need time to think how to deal with that part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. I was just curious. It's possible that the rapture is much more prominent in protestant theologies when it comes to hunters or even just ordinary Christians. It is a dark world after all.<br /> <br /> Look forward to the theories. Good luck<br /> <br /> EDIT: Small gripe. Wouldn't bijinn work as a sub movement to the Enigmatics rather than as Ashwood abbey? I see the abbey overlap, but still","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 07-20-2023, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T14:25:14-07:00","id":1518568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517906-conspiracy-theory-compacts#post1517906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main problem with them, however, is F- they just don't really have the vibes for a conspiracy. On the other hand, Campion are a conspiracy, so.. I don't know, I need to think about it more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Null Mysteriis don't really have an agenda beyond understanding what they're looking at. Sure you could give them an Endowment of study tools, but that would imply a level of understanding that their vibe tells us they're still trying to get.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Serving as a support group for monsters is a interesting niche, sure, but I'm not sure they have much in the other criteria. The main thing they have standing for them is B, yet their supernatural benefits are almost identical to the Bear Lodge- so if they get the conspiracy treatment instead of the chapter treatment, this compact has nothing in their favor. Not sure if they should be a chapter of the Survivors Club- they have some overlap, but maybe they'll work better with some other group... </div> </div> </div>I disagree that the Talbot Group would fit well into the Survivor's Club.<br /> <br /> For them to be a decent conspiracy, I think you would have to go the whole hog and say they <i>can</i> cure monstrous transformations (even if every individual monster is a separate R&amp;D-a-new-endowment). If there's no mechanically supported chance of them doing that, leave them as a compact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maiden's Blood Sisterhood:[/B] their connection to witches and the occult gives them a decent score for B, which also answers D by extension. They also seem to have enough structure to answer C, and are around 66 years old so I am willing to give them E. They do have overlap with the Survivors Club, however, so I need to give it thought (even though they are a good excuse for adapting a Cruac version for Hunter). </div> </div> </div>The text even says they have some witch members. And I think they're different enough from the Survivor's club to justify both - indeed having two groups that are historically related is interesting in itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Habibti Maa have some interesting things going on for them. There seems to be some supernatural benefit for their deprogramming techniques, which answers B, and they have Maat as their patron (which could indicate some involvement by the Judges), so we have D. I also think that C is also on the table for them. </div> </div> </div>Something like discovering an inverted Sybaris that eases supernatural compulsions and urges to worship? And which also gives them a &quot;super psychology&quot; (in the sense of superscience).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reckoning: easy no, basically fail uniqueness for the Long Night and have little to no support for any other criteria. </div> </div> </div>Plus they're ludicrously niche. It's like having a hunter group that only goes after Nosfratu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yuri's Group: again, fail on S towards the Survivors Club, and all else falls apart accordingly. </div> </div> </div>They could also be part of Habibi Ma. In fact, this group, Habibi Ma, and the Talbot Group could all blend into a conspiracy, developing an Endowment from pooling their insights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Crimson Halo: on one hand, they are community guardians. On the other, they answer the criteria much better than any other similar group. They have some answer for C, and answer E as good as any compact could, having more than 100 years on their side. They are also unique, but lack in the other fields. I would have to think about it, yet it might just be because I really love them. </div> </div> </div>I love them too, but you'd have to be the Night Watch in order to have fewer resources with which to develop an Endowment. Plus I think a critical part of their vibe is that their marginalisation and the fact that they're looking out for each other because no one else gives a shit. Making them a big conspiracy messes with that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28116-tzies","name":"Tzies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T03:15:07-07:00","id":1518904,"title":"","content":"I'll be extremely blunt when I say this:<br /> <br /> <b>Las Guadanas</b>\u200b are very clearly based off of the Adolfo Constanzo cult -- up to and including the incorrect attribution of blood/human sacrifice to Santa Muerte, when the religion in question was Palo Mayombe. They're a criminal cartel worshiping La Santa, who is a religious figure that has already been incorrectly used numerous times by individuals in various pieces of media. The fact that the writers are aware that Santa Muerte goes back to &quot;Aztec Death Cults&quot; (which is an extremely ... blase way to say that Santa Muerte is a long-practiced tradition that has been passed down through the generations) indicates that there is the capacity to do research. In particular, the nail in the coffin here is that Las Guadanas are a Santa Muerte-worshiping Drug Cartel. I don't think I need to explain what the problem is here.<br /> <br /> South America has been used consistently throughout the history of CoD/WoD as a &quot;mysterious evil death cult criminal sanctuary&quot;, for lack of a better term. To see this done yet again, to see a semi-closed faith so deliberately misrepresented, and to see people so immediately ready to just... put the pedal to the medal on this is extremely disconcerting.<br /> <br /> If you want to have a compact based off Santa Muerte belief, that's fine, but ... like, research should have been done, and <i>you really, REALLY should not have involved the cartels, especially since this is VERY clearly based off of an ACTUAL real life cult that has caused Santa Muerte to have a bad reputation. </i><br /> <br /> It gets <b>very old</b> to see, time and time again, Mexico/the Global South used as an &quot;OOOH SPOOKY SCARY OOOH CULTS OOOH BLOOD SACRIFICE&quot; zone. There's so much more to it than that, and the fact that these racist concepts are just left uncommented on and celebrated doesn't sit well with me.<br /> <br /> Las Guadanas could very easily be a supremely interesting group, playing off of the positive aspects of La Santa, and the positive views of Death in general.<br /> <br /> I don't think I'd be so frustrated if it were for the fact that the authors know She has been passed through the generations by these &quot;Aztec Death Cults&quot; (as has been so eagerly said), which means that someone like. Google searched La Santa, searched the faith, saw <b>everything else</b>, and ... decided to go with the portrayal that continues the line's use of Mexico/South America as an edgy zone for blood sacrifice, criminals, and murder.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I'm hoping that Las Guadanas is changed when it's expanded upon. It gets really, really old, seeing the same things passed off over and over again.<br /> <br /> EDITING TO ADD: I'm actually also irritated because I KNOW Onyx Path does research. Scion works with Native individuals to respectfully portray the faiths in question and the cultures involved. I KNOW OP does actually put in the work not do rehash these old offensive stereotypes with other lines. Is it just ok when it's Mexico, then? I know Hunter and Scion are different writing teams but there's something that just gets under my skin about it.<br /> <br /> I need to make it very clear, too, that part of my issue is just looking at the way South America has been treated in the canon before. While there are a few positive examples, the OVERWHELMING majority of content is... well, like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27762-jackal-alltrades","user":"Jackal Alltrades","date":". 07-27-2023, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27762-jackal-alltrades","name":"Jackal Alltrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T13:23:31-07:00","id":1518955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackal Alltrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517906-conspiracy-theory-compacts?p=1518904#post1518904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be extremely blunt when I say this:<br /> <br /> <b>Las Guadanas</b>\u200b are very clearly based off of the Adolfo Constanzo cult -- up to and including the incorrect attribution of blood/human sacrifice to Santa Muerte, when the religion in question was Palo Mayombe. They're a criminal cartel worshiping La Santa, who is a religious figure that has already been incorrectly used numerous times by individuals in various pieces of media. The fact that the writers are aware that Santa Muerte goes back to &quot;Aztec Death Cults&quot; (which is an extremely ... blase way to say that Santa Muerte is a long-practiced tradition that has been passed down through the generations) indicates that there is the capacity to do research. In particular, the nail in the coffin here is that Las Guadanas are a Santa Muerte-worshiping Drug Cartel. I don't think I need to explain what the problem is here.<br /> <br /> South America has been used consistently throughout the history of CoD/WoD as a &quot;mysterious evil death cult criminal sanctuary&quot;, for lack of a better term. To see this done yet again, to see a semi-closed faith so deliberately misrepresented, and to see people so immediately ready to just... put the pedal to the medal on this is extremely disconcerting.<br /> <br /> If you want to have a compact based off Santa Muerte belief, that's fine, but ... like, research should have been done, and <i>you really, REALLY should not have involved the cartels, especially since this is VERY clearly based off of an ACTUAL real life cult that has caused Santa Muerte to have a bad reputation. </i><br /> <br /> It gets <b>very old</b> to see, time and time again, Mexico/the Global South used as an &quot;OOOH SPOOKY SCARY OOOH CULTS OOOH BLOOD SACRIFICE&quot; zone. There's so much more to it than that, and the fact that these racist concepts are just left uncommented on and celebrated doesn't sit well with me.<br /> <br /> Las Guadanas could very easily be a supremely interesting group, playing off of the positive aspects of La Santa, and the positive views of Death in general.<br /> <br /> I don't think I'd be so frustrated if it were for the fact that the authors know She has been passed through the generations by these &quot;Aztec Death Cults&quot; (as has been so eagerly said), which means that someone like. Google searched La Santa, searched the faith, saw <b>everything else</b>, and ... decided to go with the portrayal that continues the line's use of Mexico/South America as an edgy zone for blood sacrifice, criminals, and murder.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I'm hoping that Las Guadanas is changed when it's expanded upon. It gets really, really old, seeing the same things passed off over and over again.<br /> <br /> EDITING TO ADD: I'm actually also irritated because I KNOW Onyx Path does research. Scion works with Native individuals to respectfully portray the faiths in question and the cultures involved. I KNOW OP does actually put in the work not do rehash these old offensive stereotypes with other lines. Is it just ok when it's Mexico, then? I know Hunter and Scion are different writing teams but there's something that just gets under my skin about it.<br /> <br /> I need to make it very clear, too, that part of my issue is just looking at the way South America has been treated in the canon before. While there are a few positive examples, the OVERWHELMING majority of content is... well, like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m sorry you don\u2019t like Las Guada\u00f1as. Any problems with them are solely due to me and has nothing to do with Onyx Path as a whole. I\u2019m the one who wrote them, and I take full responsibility for everything problematic about them.<br /> My intent with them was not to play on any stereotypes, and I apologize for having failed in this. I also wasn\u2019t intending to depict Las Guada\u00f1as as reflections of the real world followers of Santa Muerte. Las Guada\u00f1as are worshippers of Death, and they wrap their beliefs in the religious trappings society uses to honor Death. Even in their Aztec roots, they weren\u2019t part of the mainstream religion. When I\u2019d conceived of them, I was picturing an organized crime syndicate who were also a Death cult with the \u201csacred duty\u201d to return those who cheated Death to her loving embrace. I chose Santa Muerte because she was a popular figure, and then added the cultural connections to make her fit with them, then stretched their roots into the past so the group could have existed long enough to be bothered by immortals. My research wasn\u2019t as thorough as it should have been, nor did I manage to avoid making them into offensive stereotypes. I apologize for this, and I thank you for bringing it to my attention. I will endeavor to do better in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T15:06:52-07:00","id":1519051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517906-conspiracy-theory-compacts?p=1518955#post1518955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m sorry you don\u2019t like Las Guada\u00f1as. Any problems with them are solely due to me and has nothing to do with Onyx Path as a whole. I\u2019m the one who wrote them, and I take full responsibility for everything problematic about them.<br /> My intent with them was not to play on any stereotypes, and I apologize for having failed in this. I also wasn\u2019t intending to depict Las Guada\u00f1as as reflections of the real world followers of Santa Muerte. Las Guada\u00f1as are worshippers of Death, and they wrap their beliefs in the religious trappings society uses to honor Death. Even in their Aztec roots, they weren\u2019t part of the mainstream religion. When I\u2019d conceived of them, I was picturing an organized crime syndicate who were also a Death cult with the \u201csacred duty\u201d to return those who cheated Death to her loving embrace. I chose Santa Muerte because she was a popular figure, and then added the cultural connections to make her fit with them, then stretched their roots into the past so the group could have existed long enough to be bothered by immortals. My research wasn\u2019t as thorough as it should have been, nor did I manage to avoid making them into offensive stereotypes. I apologize for this, and I thank you for bringing it to my attention. I will endeavor to do better in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really appreciate the response, and the genuine apology. We don't see that sort of thing enough, these days.<br /> <br /> I think the root idea you have is really a good one, if it helps at all: the Death as Sacred Duty concept carries a lot of weight. Mexican faith involves the cycle of death, the soul, and rebirth, and there are a lot of ways that can be worked with! You could keep the ties of the criminal organization, but it would be best to separate that from the worship of La Santa.<br /> <br /> Honestly, your interest in the long legacy of the faith is great to see. You can find some good resources!<br /> <br /> I fully believe you can do something with this, and your apology means a lot to me and to the people impacted by this, especially in a time where we are often just defensively deflected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27762-jackal-alltrades","name":"Jackal Alltrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T16:45:10-07:00","id":1520337,"title":"","content":"God, those were some chaotic couple of weeks... Well, let's get back to this thing, shall we?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Ashwood Abbey</b></span><br /> <br /> Our dear old beloved hedonists, the Ashwood Abbey are somewhat of a divisive subject within the fandom- it looks like you either love those bastards, or hate them with passion, and it is easy to get why. There is a reason why the original Hunter 2e team have considered to unite them with the Hunt Club and make them into a full blown cabal, something I am personally happy didn't happen. There is some dark honesty with the Abbey that you can't get with other organizations- that in the end, monsters are <i>not</i> people. This is the very base of the Code, and that separation is essential for it to work. And if monsters are not people, then you should not treat them as people. And if you should not treat them as people, than it is ok to kill them, right? After all, that is the Code. And if it is ok to kill them, it is ok to harvest them, right? Cheiron are doing that, the Bear Lodge are doing that, Campion are doing that. So if you can harvest them, than clearly you can also play with them- people hunt animals all of the time. Oh, sure, you could speak about it as &quot;immoral&quot;, but in the end, hunting is just something humans do- kill for fun, and it is ok because they are not human. Heck, Shulpae even eat monsters- this is only ok if we are talking about something which is definitely not human. So if you can harvest them, hunt them for fun, eat them and so forth- why to stop here? Monsters are <i>not</i> people, and so it is ok to <i>not</i> treat them as people. And if there is some dark, sick fantasy that you have buried within the back of your mind, something you could never, ever do on another human being because it is sick and twisted- than it should be ok if you will do it on monsters, right? After all, they are <i>not</i> people. They are Fair Game.<br /> <br /> Sure, any sane person would tell you that this is taking things too far- after all, there are things which we consider to be immoral even when used against none-human entities. Animals, in Western perspective, have some rights- right to minimize their suffering, for example. Yet not everyone agree on those rights, and some people, especially those who are somewhat detached from the rest of society, have a different view on things. When you are powerful enough, the laws of society no longer apply upon you. When you have enough money, you can throw it on your problems and make it disappear. When you already have absolute control over the life of others, morality is just a thing you can bury beneath tons of hard, cold cash. And if you have those sick, twisted desires, and all of that power in the palm of your hand, wouldn't it be better that instead of practicing those desires on people, that you would do it on <i>none</i> people? And what better use there is for it than practicing them on those who actually prey on humanity and cause misfortune to others? Heck, you could probably even write it off as charity service! You should get a tax relief for that!<br /> <br /> Rich people have their own morals- just like hunters.<br /> <br /> Now, even if we are to consider the Ashwood Abbey as being composed of the rich and the powerful, it is still not enough for them to be a conspiracy- a bunch of rich people who go around and kill monsters for fun is a nice concept, but that's just it. A bunch of people. However, the Abbey is far more than that- it is not merely a social gathering, it is a Hellfire Club. Heck, it is a network of such clubs. It is a social structure aimed at allowing the platform for rich hunters to go around and kill monsters. Every hedonistic rich bastard can go around and stab vampires in parties, but doing so with the logo of the Abbey? Now, that's the extra. The Abbey is a brand, and rich people are more than happy to pay for the brand, to show that they have a class. They are not just bastards with money, they are bastards with money who can afford themselves to pay membership fees. Not only that they are playing the most dangerous game and go through highly risky parties, they either pay a significant amount of money to do so, or sometimes are being sponsored by the compact in order to do so under the brand of the Abbey. Cells of the Abbey are supervised, they have membership fees and license, and if you are to stop pay the fees, or start breaking the rules of the Hellfire Club (like, for example, starting to kill people instead of monsters), the license is being revoked. The Abbey can't let its brand to be contaminated, after all. They need to make sure it represent what they want it to represents- this is a sign that the parties are of a high quality, that the prey has been scrutinized, that the game is being well defined. And if you are using their brand without their permission- well, the Abbey would have to do something about it, and that might mean that for some very sad consequences, you are no longer counting as a person. Again, very unfortunate- but the brand must be maintained, after all.<br /> <br /> So this is the thing that is often missed about the Abbey- the rich people? They are <i>not</i> the driving power behind the compact. They are its <i>costumers</i>. The Hellfire Club is there to offer services, such as the brand, the parties, the social network and the activities (hence why the sponsor talented hunters). The Abbey is a business- and a well oiled one, too. In some ways, as C&amp;C mentions, it could be conside4red a pyramid scheme: only members of the Abbey are its own clients, who pay huge sums of money just to operate under a brand given by a mysterious sponsor. Someone makes tons of profit out of rich bastards who want to kill monsters with class, basically playing them like fools. A lot of money flows through that mechanism, and it is that mechanism, not the rich bastards, which could be the leading factor for them to become a conspiracy.<br /> <br /> But if that is the case- what is the plan?<br /> <br /> Well, rich people playing &quot;the Great Game&quot; is a trope and existing conspiracy theory which is already represented within the Abbey- so on the night to night activity, the Abbey keeps offering the same services to its costumers- and potentially focusing more on initiating Bacchanals, sponsoring competitions and talents in order to satisfy the desires of the rich people who take part in the would be conspiracy. The person at the head of the pyramid, however, might have other plans in mind- after all, they have power, money and control. As long as they decide to just let hunters to kill and get killed with style, there is nothing that needs to happen. But if they are to decide to actually do something with all of the resources they have, well, that might be the point where things would become interesting. Yet, considering that we are likely talking about someone who is very selfish and cares only on a material gain, what could make them to actually change direction in such a manner?<br /> <br /> To pay a debt, perhaps.<br /> <br /> Look, let's stop beating around the bush. This is an Hellfire Club. It is oozing with vice. Lust, greed, gluttony, wrath, pride, envy, sloth- the Abbey is all of those and more. It is a fertile ground for Whisperers to rise, to infernals to grow, and to archdemons to feed. Heck, the whole brand of the compact might serve as a testament for such a demon. The hunters of the Abbey can not be satiated, and it is very likely that some entities who watched from the cracks between worlds have learned to exploit them. After all, we are talking about people who already have everything they might wish <i>except</i> of fun, and so fun they will have. The head of the pyramid, unlike the costumers of the Abbey, might not have been born to money- instead, it might have well been someone who cut a deal with a dark being in order to gain money, and perhaps as they cut more and more deals for power, the debt for Hell grows as well, and then there is only one way to repay that debt- with souls. With blood. That, however, is unethical- you can't just sacrifice the lives of people to save yours! That's immoral!... Thankfully, the compact is specialized at finding those whoa re not people, and what better way to pay their debt than by using those monsters- and the vice that the Bacchanal produce - to satisfy the demon lords who lurk in the shadows of the conspiracy?<br /> <br /> With that scenario in mind, it also helps to define what kind of Endowments the conspiracy version of the Abbey might look like- from one end, it should be about vice, about pleasure, about sin and taint and fun. On the other, it should be about control, about resources, about the ability to throw money at the problem and get what you want. The result of that mashing of ideals should be something along the lines of <b><i>Infernal Investment</i></b> (well, they probably won't put &quot;infernal&quot; in the name, but you get the gist). The members of the conspiracy pe4rform the Vigil as an act of devotion to a demonic Testament. The acts of the Vigil become a secondary (or tertiary, in case of Vice-Ridden people) Vice, allowing them to regain special &quot;infernal&quot; Willpower, which can then be expanded upon all sorts of subtle supernatural abilities, mostly ones which control, submit, bind, twist and corrupt others. Break the will of the monster, infest it with desire, confuse, drug, devour explore, claim. Get what you want, remove what you don't. Make others touch you, do not get touched. Make the world answer your truest, darkest desires, all in the name of the Vigil. If conspiracies are about making monsters into people, then the Ashwood Abbey's are Possessed, and their infernal vestments are being worn proudly, all in the name of the Vigil. Hell has fire too, after all- and it banish the darkness all the same.<br /> <br /> Well, in that case, you might ask, what is the goal of the Ashwood Abbey?<br /> <br /> To make sure that the fun will never end.<br /> <br /> Unlike most other conspiracies, the Ashwood Abbey do not desire an end to the Vigil- there can only be fun as long as there is a Code, only as long as that some people are not people. They want a full blown, global, everlasting Bacchanal, a party which will never end, a Weirdmagedon so to speak. They want the darkness to be revealed, monsters to be driven out of the shadows, for morality to collapse and for vice to overflow the world. A world where the strong control, where the weak obey, where passion is currency and all live in their desire. A world overridden by monsters and hunters, all of which dance while the Abbey looks on the burning world with pleasure. The Ashwood Abbey wants a Hell upon Earth- and when the streets will be soaked red, when the gates of Hell will be breached, when desires will take form in flesh and the legions of Inferno will march upon the world, those who are able to pay the fees will be spared, will the others will become monsters through Hell's foul touch. And how can they pay the debt? Money? No, you fool- Hell has no use for money. Blood. Pain. Desire. Souls. That's the currency. Practice the Vigil, join the Bacchanal, and Hell will spare you- for as long as you pay the debt. Refuse, and you will be a Fair Game. Live in your sin- that's how the debt will be paid.<br /> <br /> Rich people have their own morals.<br /> <br /> Like Hunters.<br /> <br /> Like Demons.<br /> <br /> ************************************************** *********************<br /> <br /> Finally, some break to sit and write. This was a fun bit- I hope you enjoyed it, and stay tuned for the next pieces in this project!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T17:20:02-07:00","id":1520342,"title":"","content":"Ahh, a purely evil end game. No noble intentions, no deluded justification, no paradise through immoral means, just selfish indulgence at the cost of the lesser. Very refreshing. Nice involvement of the Possessed. Been a while.<br /> <br /> Also, I've always liked to imagine the man at the top of the Abbey is nothing more than a pathetic wretch trying to keep himself safe from the outside world. Your suggestion is very easy to reconcile with that view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T05:50:52-07:00","id":1520378,"title":"","content":"add to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1473351-conspiracy-theory-hub-thread\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...ory-hub-thread</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T07:18:08-07:00","id":1520385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phoenix853457</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517906-conspiracy-theory-compacts?p=1520378#post1520378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">add to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1473351-conspiracy-theory-hub-thread\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...ory-hub-thread</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I will update when I'll have time, don't worry. No need to send me messages everywhere :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T15:46:18-07:00","id":1520417,"title":"","content":"It has been awhile since I've read Inferno. Are infernal vestments the abilities of the Possessed, or are they meant to replace the Bacchanal as the Endowment of the Ashwood Abbey?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T14:12:37-07:00","id":1521064,"title":"","content":"After watching John Wick 4 it occurred to me that if you wanted to put a Continental Hotel in a Hunter game, Ashwood Abbey would make perfect sense for a group to run it; I could imagine them handing out memberships to particular Hunters who catch their eye, even if they aren't members of the Compact proper.<br /> <br /> Also, apropos of nothing, if enough Conspirators from TF:V, VASCU, and Project Nebula got together you'd have a little baby XCOM. Maybe Cheiron too, to cover the biological augments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T07:17:21-07:00","id":1538900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517906-conspiracy-theory-compacts?p=1520337#post1520337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Make others touch you, do not get touched.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Ballad of Tam Lin, Bonnie Janet wants to meet Tam, so she deliberately violates a faerie prohibition so she'll owe him sex.<br /> <br /> As the &quot;haves&quot; of the ordinary world and very much the &quot;have-nots&quot; of the secret world, Ashwood Abbey should always be trying to scam for occult power.<br /> <br /> I don't see Ashwood Abbey ever being a Conspiracy - that's far too stable and coordinated. And I think they ought to have about a dozen &quot;inner circles,&quot; none of which are actually in charge. V,VIP clubs that keep out the mere VIPs. Some are local, some reach as far as the Compact itself.<br /> <br /> The Coleridge Club: A Kiss-addicted cell were trawling for hot vampires and snagged a Daeva of the Anvari bloodline. Anvari, who have a particular relationship with opiates, normally try to spend at least every third night on the natch, but the Abbey are <i>such </i>enablers - this vampire hasn't been off the opiates in <i>decades</i>. The cell are all ghouls now, sincerely devoted to their master who, however, is obviously incompetent. &quot;Come on, Master, let's get you cleaned up,&quot; without a trace of irony. The vampire is their god, the image of their god, and their blood refinery. They use their borrowed Discipline of Nepenthe to build a web of influence that makes them almost untouchable - and when that doesn't work, the superhuman strength and speed come in handy.<br /> <br /> (Daniel) Webster's Dictionary: Sure, why not infernal contracts? But always stay on top. They don't practice soul trade - they make short term contracts with infernal demons, at the low, low price of aggravated damage. And they are very good at it. But the practice is addictive, and none of them can stop.<br /> <br /> Likely at least one Necromantic Cult (as per Geist) nestled within each clique - Elysians among the Competitors, Necropolitans among the Libertines, and Thanatologists among the Pursuit. Harmless (or amusing) ghosts get fed Essence for spying, doing tricks, or serving as research subjects; dangerous (or boring) ghosts get turned into Mementos for the arsenal - or even just the museum.<br /> <br /> Ceremonial Thaumaturges, because of course. That's the least unusual method of parlaying wealth and leisure into occult power.<br /> <br /> Those Mentors that Enigmatics get at Status ***? <i>Be </i>one of those.<br /> <br /> To return to the beginning, Fae-Touched. Make a binding promise to an interesting person and have a kick-ass magical-world adventure? What did <i>you</i> have penciled in for Friday? They'd do this even if it <i>didn't</i> get them scraps of magic.<br /> <br /> The temptation to do <i>all</i> of these things is pretty strong, and there's no reason an Abbey hunter shouldn't be allowed to try. It spreads the Experiences pretty thin, and it creates conflicting obligations, but sure, go for it. Here's a little secret - Ashwood Abbey hunters are some of the characters who are closest to knowing the rules of the game the players are playing. Conflicting obligations are <i>time in the spotlight</i>. Horrible experiences are <i>Beats</i>. And while the Abbey are the only Hunter characters who hunt for entertainment, all Hunter players are playing Hunter for entertainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-20T15:30:14-07:00","id":1538954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517906-conspiracy-theory-compacts?p=1521064#post1521064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After watching John Wick 4 it occurred to me that if you wanted to put a Continental Hotel in a Hunter game, Ashwood Abbey would make perfect sense for a group to run it; I could imagine them handing out memberships to particular Hunters who catch their eye, even if they aren't members of the Compact proper.<br /> <br /> Also, apropos of nothing, if enough Conspirators from TF:V, VASCU, and Project Nebula got together you'd have a little baby XCOM. Maybe Cheiron too, to cover the biological augments.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still say that Nebula will never, ever work with TF:V. TF:V <i>are</i> the heavy hand of the Federal government, sneaking around in black helicopters - a nightmare for the Nebuloids worse than the invaders themselves. Okay, so they get jerked around a bit by ADAMSKI. Okay, so they have a tiny bit of sincere, but arm's-length, cooperation with FORT. Okay, so if they followed leads to the same problem, they'd fight it more than they'd fight each other - probably. They won't work together. Ever. Like, the subject of an entire chronicle would be getting some of them to talk to one another other than in dark warehouses with voice scramblers.<br /> <br /> I'm having Nebula get together with the White Hare Society, then re-split along ideological lines. I think that's a fruitful idea.<br /> <br /> VASCU and TF:V should work together, and slice up the areas of responsibility a little better than they did in as written up in Slashers. Maybe they do bring Division 6 on board as well.<br /> <br /> The Barrett Commission? It doesn't exist, never existed, and <i>certainly</i> never had a budget. It's called the Barrett Commission in Night Stalkers simply because they had to have some kind of name to have a write-up. It's a few hundred people, most of whom have never met - or never met <i>knowingly</i>. Some of them know one another outside the conspiracy (small &quot;c&quot; is intentional) and don't know that the person on the other end of the dead-drop is also a colleague in their public activities. Those dead-drops? They are of encrypted thumb drives, and they get passed by dead-drop once to a courier, who doesn't have the key and who copies the drive and destroys the original, and then passed by another dead-drop to the recipient. The courier never knows who's on either end of the chain. Why not deliver the original? Because vampires can smell your fingerprints or something, and they've lost people that way. (That's right, Barrett doesn't even know about Auspex, but they try to beat it anyway.)<br /> <br /> Of course the Barrett Commission (which, remember, doesn't exist) have their hooks into TF:V. They put hits on vampires, then watch which ones are disallowed. Vampires TF:V are not allowed to whack get further scrutiny - they are presumably the secret masters themselves, their pawns, or their friends. You could make a map of the vampire conspiracy that way. They mostly let those vampires alone, except for extremely discreet observation, against the day when they have enough information for a clean sweep. But if a particular vampire is an immediate danger, they'll activate a Barrett associate embedded in a Tier 1 or 2 cell, who &quot;discovers&quot; that vampire and tries to get his buddies to come along for the hit. Barrett hunters, as a class, loathe Ashwood Abbey, but they're not above having some of their people coat-trail to get recruited, just because the Ashwoods tend to have better equipment than most Tier 2 hunters. These Barrett hunters have a tendency to go &quot;native&quot; after a while, but that's all right - they didn't know enough to betray the Commission.<br /> <br /> I can't recommend playing as a member of the Barrett Commission - that's not a storytelling game, it's a worker-placement board game. But they're out there (except of course that they aren't, because they don't exist) working for you and me. Approximately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T05:08:02-07:00","id":1539015,"title":"","content":"Why are the Recalibrators even called that? Because they are already doing a bit of subtle regular-people magic. It's not too different from the 1E Corruption and Defile tactics. When they clean a scene, they also abjure its temporal sympathy all the way down to Weak, without having to resort to radical physical damage. This also makes the scene's related unclaimed Chamber in the Primordial Dream detach and fall into the Mists, and if the scene was a ghost's Anchor, it isn't any more.<br /> Do they know what they're doing? Maybe not. But someone must know. Someone is fighting the dream war with Lysol and hope.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's just my take. But it's a take so obvious, at least to me, that the first time I read TtF, I was surprised to get through the Recalibrators entry without reading something like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}